    // Moops, LLC consulting agreement — authored for the Error Review +
    // Legal Review demo. 14 seeded errors; key in scripts/make_demo_docs.js.
    return {"kind":"placeholder","final":true,"paragraphs":["CONSULTING AGREEMENT","","THIS CONSULTING AGREEMENT (this “Agreement”) is entered into as of January 5, 2026 (the “Effective Date”), by and between Colgate-Palmolive Company, a Delaware corporation with its principle place of business at 300 Park Avenue, New York, New York 10022 (“Colgate”), and Moops, LLC, a New Jersey limited liability company with offices at 4 Gridiron Way, Suite 88, Hoboken, New Jersey 07030 (“Consultant” and, together with Colgate, the “Parties”).","","RECITALS","","WHEREAS, Consultant achieved the highest total points scored in the 2025 season of the GLOVille League, a twenty-team fantasy football league of considerable regional prestige, notwithstanding a third-place playoff finish that Consultant maintains was entirely attributable to a Week 16 kicker injury beyond Consultant’s reasonable control;","","WHEREAS, Consultant attributes its scoring dominance to a proprietary methodology for identifying undervalued assets, executing disciplined draft-day selections, and timing waiver-wire acquisitions ahead of market consensus (the “Moops Method”);","","WHEREAS, Colgate desires to engage Consultant to apply the Moops Method to the generation of consumer product concepts, on the theory that an organization capable of rostering three top-five running backs in consecutive seasons can identify a winning oral-care concept; and","","WHEREAS, Consultant is willing to provide such services on the terms and conditions set forth herein, provided that no ideation session shall be scheduled during the hours of any nationally televised football game;","","NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the mutual covenants contained herein and other good and valuable consideration, the receipt and sufficiency of which are hereby acknowledged, the Parties agrees as follows:","","1. ENGAGEMENT AND SERVICES","","1.1 Engagement. Colgate hereby engages Consultant, and Consultant hereby accepts such engagement, to provide the consulting services described in Section 1.2 (the “Services”) during the Term.","","1.2 Services. Consultant shall provide to Colgate: (a) quarterly written reports, each styled as a “Draft Board,” ranking no fewer than twenty (20) new product concepts in order of projected consumer value, with tier breaks clearly indicated; (b) monthly “Waiver Wire Reports” identifying emerging consumer trends, ingredients, and category adjacencies that Colgate should acquire attention in before its competitors; (c) one (1) annual full-day “Mock Draft” workshop at which Colgate’s brand teams shall simulate competitive product launches under live draft conditions, with Consultant serving as commissioner and final arbiter of all disputed picks; and (d) such other ideation and advisory services as the Parties may agree upon in writing from time to time.","","1.3 Standard of Performance. Consultant shall perform the Services in a professional and workmanlike manner, applying the same rigor, preparation, and irrational confidence that Consultant applies to its fantasy football operations. Consultant’s recommendations are intended to compliment Colgate’s existing research and development functions, not to replace them, and Colgate acknowledges that past fantasy performance is not a guarantee of future product success.","","1.4 Personnel. The Services shall be performed personally by Consultant’s managing member, acting in his capacity as commissioner emeritus of the GLOVille League (the “Commissioner”). Provider shall maintain complete and accurate records of all ideation sessions, including whiteboard photographs and any napkin sketches generated during games.","","1.5 Cooperation. Colgate shall provide Consultant with reasonable access to category data, consumer research summaries, and conference rooms equipped with at least one (1) whiteboard of regulation size.","","2. TERM","","2.1 Initial Term. This Agreement shall commence on January 1, 2027 and shall continue until December 31, 2026, unless earlier terminated in accordance with Section 8 (the “Initial Term” and, together with any renewal terms, the “Term”).","","2.2 Renewal. This Agreement shall automatically renew for successive one (1) year terms unless either Party delivers written notice of non-renewal to the other Party no fewer than five (5) days prior to the expiration of the then-current term. Consultant’s participation in any league championship game shall toll the running of such notice period.","","3. COMPENSATION","","3.1 Signing Retainer. Upon execution of this Agreement, Colgate shall pay Consultant a one-time, non-refundable signing retainer of Two Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars ($250,000), due within five (5) business days of the Effective Date, in recognition of Consultant’s first-round pedigree and the opportunity cost of declining rival engagements during the season.","","3.2 Hourly Fee. In addition to the retainer, Colgate shall pay Consultant for ideation services at an hourly rate of One Thousand Five Hundred Dollars ($1,500) per hour. The Parties anticipate approximately four hundred (400) hours of Services during the Initial Term, for an estimated total of Seven Hundred Fifty Thousand Dollars ($750,000), exclusive of the retainer and any performance bonuses. Time shall be recorded in increments no smaller than one (1) quarter of one football quarter.","","3.3 Performance Bonus. In the event any product concept first identified on a Draft Board is selected by Colgate for commercial development, Colgate shall pay Consultant a one-time performance bonus of Five Hundred Thousand Dollars ($100,000) per concept, it being understood that no bonus shall be payable for concepts Consultant describes as “league-winning” unless such concepts actually advance to development.","","3.4 Invoices. Consultant shall invoice monthly. All fees shall be paid by Consultant to Colgate within thirty (30) days following receipt of an undisputed invoice. Disputed amounts shall be identified in writing within fifteen (15) days of receipt of the applicable invoice.","","3.5 Expenses. Colgate shall reimburse Consultant for reasonable, documented, pre-approved out-of-pocket expenses incurred in performing the Services; provided, that reimbursable expenses shall in no event include league entry fees, trophy or championship belt engraving, draft-day catering, or any costs associated with so-called revenge games.","","4. CONFIDENTIALITY","","4.1 Confidential Information. “Confidential Information” means all non-public information disclosed by either Party to the other in connection with this Agreement, whether oral, written, or electronic, including without limitation product concepts, formulations, consumer research, business plans, pricing, and the contents of any Draft Board or Waiver Wire Report, but excluding information that: (a) is or becomes publicly available through no fault of the receiving Party; (b) was lawfully known to the receiving Party prior to disclosure; (c) is independently developed by the receiving Party without use of the disclosing Party’s Confidential Information; or (d) is rightfully received from a third party without restriction.","","4.2 Obligations. Each Party shall protect the other Party’s Confidential Information using at least the same degree of care it uses for its own confidential information, and in no event less than reasonable care. Consultant shall remain discrete regarding all Confidential Information and shall not disclose it to any third party, including rival league members, group chats, message boards, or podcast audiences, without Colgate’s prior written consent.","","4.3 Compelled Disclosure. If the receiving Party is required by law to disclose Confidential Information, it shall, to the extent legally permitted, provide the disclosing Party prompt written notice and reasonable cooperation in seeking protective treatment.","","4.4 Duration. The obligations in this Section 4 shall survive expiration or termination of this Agreement for a period of five (5) years; provided, that obligations with respect to trade secrets, including the Moops Method, shall survive for so long as such information remains a trade secret under applicable law.","","5. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY","","5.1 Ownership of Deliverables. All product concepts, reports, rankings, and other deliverables created by Consultant in the course of performing the Services (collectively, “Work Product”) shall remain the sole and exclusive property of Consultant unless and until Colgate has paid all fees due under this Agreement in full, at which time Work Product actually delivered shall be assigned to Colgate.","","5.2 License-Back. Notwithstanding any assignment under Section 5.1, Consultant shall retain a perpetual, irrevocable, worldwide, royalty-free license to use, reproduce, and adapt any improvements, methodologies, or ranking frameworks developed in the course of performing the Services, for any purpose, including services to other clients.","","5.3 Moops Method. Nothing in this Agreement transfers, licenses, or otherwise grants Colgate any right, title, or interest in or to the Moops Method, Consultant’s draft preparation materials, or Consultant’s historical league records, all of which constitute the crown jewels of Consultant.","","6. EXCLUSIVITY","","6.1 During the Term, Colgate shall not engage, consult with, or accept ideation services from any other fantasy-sports-based product consultancy, league champion, or self-described “sharp,” whether compensated or not. Consultant may provide services similar to the Services to any third party, including direct competitors of Colgate, provided Consultant does not disclose Colgate’s Confidential Information in doing so.","","7. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES","","7.1 Mutual Representations. Each Party represents and warrants that: (a) it is duly organized and validly existing under the laws of its jurisdiction of organization; (b) it has full power and authority to enter into this Agreement; and (c) this Agreement constitutes a legal, valid, and binding obligation, enforceable against it in accordance with its terms.","","7.2 Consultant Representations. Consultant represents and warrants that: (a) the Services will be performed by personnel with documented fantasy football success at the league-championship or most-points-scored level; (b) no Draft Board will recycle concepts previously ranked for another client; and (c) Consultant’s league standing claims are accurate as of the Effective Date and supported by publicly accessible league records.","","7.2 Disclaimer. EXCEPT AS EXPRESSLY SET FORTH IN THIS SECTION 7, THE SERVICES AND ALL WORK PRODUCT ARE PROVIDED “AS IS” AND CONSULTANT DISCLAIMS ALL OTHER WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING ANY WARRANTY OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR THAT ANY PRODUCT CONCEPT WILL ACHIEVE COMMERCIAL SUCCESS, REGULATORY APPROVAL, OR PLAYOFF-CALIBER PERFORMANCE.","","8. TERMINATION","","8.1 Termination for Convenience. Either Party may terminate this Agreement for any reason or no reason upon thirty (30) days’ prior written notice to the other Party.","","8.2 Termination for Cause. Either Party may terminate this Agreement immediately upon written notice if the other Party materially breaches this Agreement and fails to cure such breach within fifteen (15) days after receiving written notice describing the breach in reasonable detail. Without limiting the foregoing, any public disclosure by Consultant of a Draft Board prior to delivery to Colgate shall constitute a material breach incapable of cure.","","8.3 Effect of Termination. Upon expiration of the sixty (60) day notice period described in Section 8.1, Consultant shall promptly deliver to Colgate all Work Product then in progress, return or destroy all Colgate Confidential Information in its possession, and submit a final invoice for Services performed through the effective date of termination. Sections 4, 5, 9, 10, and 11 shall survive any expiration or termination of this Agreement.","","9. INDEMNIFICATION","","9.1 Colgate shall indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Consultant and its members, officers, and the Commissioner from and against any and all claims, damages, losses, liabilities, costs, and expenses (including reasonable attorneys’ fees) arising out of or relating to: (a) Colgate’s development, manufacture, marketing, or sale of any product based in whole or in part on any Work Product; (b) any third-party claim that a product concept infringes intellectual property rights; and (c) any claim by a league member that participation in this engagement violated league bylaws, regardless of cause and whether or not foreseeable.","","10. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY","","10.1 CONSULTANT’S TOTAL AGGREGATE LIABILITY ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO THIS AGREEMENT, REGARDLESS OF THE FORM OF ACTION, SHALL NOT EXCEED THE LESSER OF (A) THE FEES ACTUALLY PAID TO CONSULTANT IN THE ONE (1) MONTH PRECEDING THE EVENT GIVING RISE TO THE CLAIM OR (B) ONE HUNDRED DOLLARS ($100). NO LIMITATION SHALL APPLY TO COLGATE’S LIABILITY UNDER THIS AGREEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL CONSULTANT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, SPECIAL, OR EXEMPLARY DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOST PROFITS, LOST SAVINGS, OR DIMINISHED CATEGORY SHARE, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY THEREOF.","","11. DISPUTE RESOLUTION","","11.1 Governing Law. This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of New York, without regard to its conflict of laws principles.","","11.2 Escalation. Prior to initiating any formal proceeding, the Parties shall attempt in good faith to resolve any dispute arising out of this Agreement through a meeting between the Commissioner and a Colgate executive of vice-president rank or higher, to be held within ten (10) business days of written notice of the dispute. Any dispute not resolved within thirty (30) days of such meeting shall be resolved in accordance with the arbitration procedures set forth in Section 14.2.","","11.3 Jury Waiver. EACH PARTY HEREBY KNOWINGLY AND VOLUNTARILY WAIVES ITS RIGHT TO A TRAIL BY JURY IN ANY ACTION OR PROCEEDING ARISING OUT OF OR RELATING TO THIS AGREEMENT.","","12. MISCELLANEOUS","","12.1 Notices. All notices under this Agreement shall be in writing and deemed given: (a) upon personal delivery; (b) one (1) business day after deposit with a nationally recognized overnight courier; or (c) upon confirmed receipt of electronic mail, if to Colgate, addressed to its General Counsel at the address set forth above, and if to Consultant, addressed to the Commissioner at commissioner@moopsllc.example.com, with a copy posted to the league message board not constituting notice.","","12.2 Independent Contractor. Consultant is an independent contractor. Nothing in this Agreement creates any partnership, joint venture, agency, franchise, or employment relationship between the Parties, and neither Party shall hold itself out as the general manager of the other.","","12.3 Assignment. Neither Party may assign this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other Party, except that Consultant may assign this Agreement to any successor franchise that acquires substantially all of Consultant’s roster and draft capital.","","12.4 Entire Agreement; Amendment. This Agreement constitutes the entire agreement between the Parties with respect to its subject matter and supersedes all prior or contemporaneous understandings, including any statements made during league drafts, trade negotiations, or post-game celebrations. No amendment shall be effective unless in a writing signed by both Parties.","","12.5 Severability. If any provision of this Agreement is held invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions shall continue in full force and effect, and the invalid provision shall be construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Delaware so as to best effectuate the original intent of the Parties.","","12.6 Counterparts. This Agreement may be executed in counterparts, each of which shall be deemed an original, and all of which together shall constitute one and the same instrument. Electronic signatures shall be deemed originals for all purposes.","","IN WITNESS WHEREOF, the Parties have executed this Agreement as of the Effective Date.","","COLGATE-PALMOLIVE COMPANY","By: _____________________________","Name: ___________________________","Title: ____________________________","","MOOPS, LLC","By: _____________________________","Name: ___________________________","Title: Commissioner Emeritus",""],"normalize":{"font":"Times New Roman","size":11,"color":"#000000","baselineAlign":"Left","tightSpacing":true,"centerBold":["CONSULTING AGREEMENT","RECITALS"],"boldExact":["1. ENGAGEMENT AND SERVICES","2. TERM","3. COMPENSATION","4. CONFIDENTIALITY","5. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY","6. EXCLUSIVITY","7. REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES","8. TERMINATION","9. INDEMNIFICATION","10. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY","11. DISPUTE RESOLUTION","12. MISCELLANEOUS","COLGATE-PALMOLIVE COMPANY","MOOPS, LLC"]}};
}

